version: "2.0"
name: gnomon-kernel-sandbox
description: >-
  The kernel sandbox profiles (darwin sandbox-exec) for what it spawns: the
  gnomon-web transport (transport.ts), sessions, mods, loop checks and loop acts
  (session.ts, mod.ts, loop-check.ts, loop-act.ts).
context:
  - >-
    Split out of packages/gnomon/.purpose (2026-10-27); path: values stay
    relative to packages/gnomon, the package root.
components:
  oracle-sandbox:
    description: >-
      #oracle-sandbox (spec §15.5) — the kernel's sandbox profiles. M1.4
      lands the `transport` profile for gnomon-web (src/kernel/sandbox/
      transport.ts): profile data, the darwin sandbox-exec SBPL generator
      (default-deny; read of `/`, /usr/lib, /System/Library, the node binary
      and its install's lib/ — never the prefix — plus Homebrew's Cellar, opt
      and etc/openssl@3; refused `sandbox-unavailable` if any granted read
      subpath equals or contains $HOME, the gnomon home or its keys dir
      (Aegis C2);
      the child's entry dir and package.json ancestors, the pinned bundle;
      metadata of their ancestors; sysctl-read; exec of node only; NO
      network-* rule at all (no bind, no inbound, no outbound — the kernel
      listens and hands connected sockets over the IPC channel,
      T-2026-10-18-020); no fork, no write, no mach-lookup; every path
      realpath'd; env empty; TRANSPORT_PROFILE v2). Platform registry TRANSPORT_BACKENDS
      (G-WIN-05): darwin only; win32 is the Windows parity phase (P8-D78);
      any platform without a backend refuses `sandbox-unavailable` (fail
      closed). Residuals: ancestor metadata is visible; node may re-exec
      itself; the child reads and writes the sockets it is handed.
      T-2026-10-18-017 (measured): SBPL accepts only `*` or `localhost` as a
      network host, and `(local ip "localhost:*")` matches every address
      configured on this host's interfaces (LAN and wildcards included), so
      no listen rule can be loopback-only. T-2026-10-18-020 (Aegis ruling)
      therefore removed every network-* rule: the kernel listens on 127.0.0.1
      and passes the CONNECTED socket (never the listening fd, whose listen()
      would be re-checked). Falsifiers in web-sandbox.test.ts: every child
      bind/listen/UDP/outbound/unix attempt EPERM against an unsandboxed
      control; a handed socket serves HTTP + a WebSocket round trip; the en0
      address at the endpoint port is refused; the SBPL names no network
      rule. The T-017 loopback-listen retry is gone (nothing left to flake).
      The other seven profiles land with their milestones (session M1.7,
      oracle M2.3, …).
    path: src/kernel/sandbox/
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, kernel, sandbox, paradigm-8, m1-4]
    tests:
      - test/web-sandbox.test.ts
      - test/web-units.test.ts
    oracles: [G-WEB-07]
